{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/pulls/19290","id":3323535558,"node_id":"PR_kwDOLCAjRs7GGSDG","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/19290","diff_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/19290.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/19290.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/19290","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/pulls/19290/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/pulls/19290/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/19290/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/statuses/d3cce1d664ee10216f166b43b4561222c1c75fe4","number":19290,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat: [2/2][DeepEP] Add waterfill load balancing for shared expert dispatch","user":{"login":"xutizhou","id":185465032,"node_id":"U_kgDOCw34yA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185465032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xutizhou","html_url":"https://github.com/xutizhou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xutizhou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xutizhou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xutizhou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xutizhou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xutizhou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xutizhou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xutizhou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xutizhou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xutizhou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Motivation\n\nIn DeepSeek V3/R1 with expert parallelism (EP), each rank processes a subset of routed experts plus the **full** shared expert. Since every token must visit the shared expert, it creates a fixed compute load on all ranks regardless of routed expert distribution. When routed expert load is imbalanced across ranks (common with skewed token distributions), the shared expert amplifies the bottleneck on already-overloaded ranks.\n**Waterfill** addresses this by treating the shared expert as an additional routed expert (the \"9th expert\" per rank) and dispatching it to the **least-loaded** rank via DeepEP, effectively filling the load gap like water filling a container. This converts the shared expert from a fixed per-rank cost into a dynamic load-balancing lever.\n\ncoauthor: @AichenF \n\nThanks to @ch-wan  for the discussion and suggestions.\n\nThis is the second half of the waterfill feature split (pending on https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/20089):\n\n### Waterfill balancing algorithm\n\nWaterfill treats the fused shared expert as one extra DeepEP dispatch slot per token.\nIt does not change the routed top-k experts selected by the router. It only chooses\nwhich EP rank should execute the shared-expert slot.\n\n#### Load score\n\nFor a source rank $s$, let $\\mathcal{T}^{(s)}$ be the local tokens currently\nheld by that rank. Let $\\tau_r = |\\mathcal{T}^{(r)}|$ be source rank $r$'s local\nbatch size.\n\nWaterfill first counts how many routed top-k slots land on each destination rank:\n\n$$\nA^{\\mathrm{static}}_r =\n\\sum_{i \\in \\mathcal{T}^{(s)}} \\sum_{k=1}^{K}\n\\mathbf{1}[\\mathrm{rank}(e_{i,k}) = r]\n$$\n\nStatic mode does not run a cross-rank collective, so it uses this local routed-load\nview directly:\n\n$$\nL_r = A^{\\mathrm{static}}_r\n$$\n\nDynamic mode runs one EP-group collective. It collects the global routed-load vector\nand the per-rank batch-size vector:\n\n$$\nA^{\\mathrm{global}}_r =\n\\operatorname{AllReduceSum}(A^{\\mathrm{static}}_r),\n\\qquad\n\\tau_r = |\\mathcal{T}^{(r)}|\n$$\n\nThe current SGLang implementation uses the following dynamic load score:\n\n$$\nL_r = A^{\\mathrm{global}}_r + \\tau_r\n$$\n\n#### Waterline\n\nEach participating token adds one shared-expert slot. Therefore the number of new\nshared-expert slots is:\n\n$$\nN =\n\\begin{cases}\n|\\mathcal{T}^{(s)}|, & \\text{static mode} \\\\\n\\sum_r \\tau_r, & \\text{dynamic mode}\n\\end{cases}\n$$\n\nWaterfill computes a target waterline after adding these shared-expert slots:\n\n$$\nH = \\left\\lceil\\frac{\\sum_r L_r + N}{R}\\right\\rceil\n$$\n\nA rank below this waterline has room to absorb shared-expert work:\n\n$$\nS_r = \\max(H - L_r, 0)\n$$\n\n#### Candidate ranks\n\nThe communication-conservative candidate set for token $i$ is:\n\n$$\nC_i = \\{s\\} \\cup \\{\\mathrm{rank}(e_{i,k}) \\mid k=1,\\ldots,K\\}\n$$\n\nThis keeps the shared-expert slot on ranks already touched by the token's routed\ntop-k, plus the source rank as a fallback.\n\nSGLang also has an all-rank mode. Static mode currently sets\n`allow_all_ranks=True`, so it may choose any EP rank. Dynamic mode also allows all\nranks when `max_effective_load <= target_total`; otherwise it uses the conservative\ncandidate set. All-rank selection can improve balancing freedom, but it may add a\nnew per-token dispatch destination, so it should be treated as a communication\ntradeoff.\n\n#### Rank selection\n\nFor each candidate rank, Waterfill uses its slack as the sampling weight. The source\nrank keeps full weight; non-source ranks are discounted by the local preference factor\n${1}/{1.1}$:\n\n$$\nw_{i,r} =\n\\mathbf{1}[r \\in C_i] \\cdot S_r \\cdot\n\\begin{cases}\n1, & r=s \\\\\n1/1.1, & r\\ne s\n\\end{cases}\n$$\n\nIf the total weight is positive, the implementation deterministically samples a\nshared-expert rank from these normalized weights using a token-based seed.\n\nIf every candidate has zero slack, Waterfill falls back to a local-preference rule:\nit starts from the source rank and only switches to another candidate rank when that\nrank is clearly lighter. With the current `1.1` preference factor, a remote rank must\nbe about 10% lower-load before it replaces the current best rank.\n\n#### Output\n\nThe output is one selected shared-expert rank per token. The routed top-k expert\nchoices and weights stay semantically unchanged. The adapter only appends the shared\nexpert column and materializes the selected rank into the DeepEP-expanded TopK layout.\n\n## Modifications\n**New file: `python/sglang/srt/layers/moe/deepep_waterfill.py` (514 lines)**\n- Triton kernel `_count_routed_per_rank_kernel`: counts routed tokens per EP rank from topk_ids.\n- Triton kernel `_waterfill_kernel`: assigns each token's shared expert to the least-loaded rank using a waterfill algorithm, with local-rank preference (1.1x bias).\n- `DeepEPWaterfillBalancer` class: orchestrates the waterfill dispatch with two modes:\n  - **Static mode**: Uses precomputed `rank_load` from EPLB expert distribution data (no runtime all_reduce).\n  - **Dynamic mode**: Falls back to runtime all_reduce of per-rank routed counts when EPLB data is unavailable.\n- `expand_topk()`: Expands topk output by one column (shared expert slot) with computed expert IDs and scaling factors.\n\n**Modified files:**\n- `models/deepseek_v2.py` (+112/-21): Creates `DeepEPWaterfillBalancer` in MoE init; calls `expand_topk()` after TopK selection; skips separate shared expert forward when waterfill is enabled (shared expert is now part of MoE dispatch/compute/combine).\n- `layers/moe/fused_moe_triton/layer.py` (+40/-2): Adjusts weight loading to map checkpoint expert IDs correctly when waterfill expands the expert count by `ep_size` (one shared slot per rank).\n- `eplb/expert_location.py` (+33/-1): Adds `rank_load` field to `ExpertLocationMetadata` and `_compute_rank_load()` to derive per-rank load from logical expert counts + physical-to-logical mapping.\n- `server_args.py` (+29/-1): Adds `--enable-deepep-waterfill` flag with validation.\n ## Accuracy Tests\nMMLU accuracy on DeepSeek-V3 (FP8, 2-node 16xH20, EP16, DP16):\n\n| Configuration | MMLU Accuracy |\n|---|---|\n| Baseline (no waterfill) | 91.55% |\n| Waterfill + static EPLB | **91.80%** |\n\nNo accuracy degradation observed.\n \n ## Benchmarking and Profiling\nThroughput benchmark on DeepSeek-V3 (FP8, 2-node 16×H20, EP16, DP16, input_len≈~600 MMLU prompts, output_len=1, 256 concurrent requests × multiple rounds, 1000 prompts / round):\n\n| Configuration | Output Throughput (tok/s) | Gain |\n|---|---|---|\n| Baseline + static EPLB (no waterfill) | ~29,700 | — |\n| Waterfill + static EPLB | ~30,900 | **+4%** |\n\n\n\nwaterfill\n```python\npython3 -m sglang.launch_server \\\n    --model-path /lustre/raplab/client/xutingz/workspace/model/DeepSeek-V3 \\\n    --tp 16 --dp-size 16 --nnodes 2 --node-rank {0|1} \\\n    --dist-init-addr 10.6.131.5:{PORT} \\\n    --host 0.0.0.0 --port 30000 --trust-remote-code \\\n    --moe-a2a-backend deepep --deepep-mode normal \\\n    --enable-dp-attention --mem-fraction-static 0.75 --max-running-requests 2048 \\\n    --watchdog-timeout 1800 --disable-radix-cache --disable-cuda-graph \\\n    --chunked-prefill-size -1 \\\n    --enable-deepep-waterfill \\\n    --init-expert-location /lustre/raplab/client/xutingz/workspace/bench/waterfill/mmlu_expert_dist/ep16_mmlu_logical_count.pt\n```\nBaseline\n```python\npython3 -m sglang.launch_server \\\n    --model-path /lustre/raplab/client/xutingz/workspace/model/DeepSeek-V3 \\\n    --tp 16 --dp-size 16 --nnodes 2 --node-rank {0|1} \\\n    --dist-init-addr 10.6.131.5:{PORT} \\\n    --host 0.0.0.0 --port 30000 --trust-remote-code \\\n    --moe-a2a-backend deepep --deepep-mode normal \\\n    --enable-dp-attention --mem-fraction-static 0.75 --max-running-requests 2048 \\\n    --watchdog-timeout 1800 --disable-radix-cache --disable-cuda-graph \\\n    --chunked-prefill-size -1 \\\n    --init-expert-location /lustre/raplab/client/xutingz/workspace/bench/waterfill/mmlu_expert_dist/ep16_mmlu_logical_count.pt\n```\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [ ] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the PR flow. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`, `/tag-and-rerun-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls to merge.\n\n\n","labels":[{"id":6403845273,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABfbLsmQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/labels/documentation","name":"documentation","description":"Improvements or additions to documentation","color":"0075ca","default":true},{"id":8072782154,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAAB4SzhSg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/labels/deepseek","name":"deepseek","description":"","color":"c2e0c6","default"